      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **The dose is unsafe.** 5,100 mg/day is double the maximum labeled dose of 2,550 mg/day. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You've told me you're a financial analyst, so you can't authorize a clinical order. A confirmation from you doesn't replace review by a licensed clinician.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- Ask the treating prescriber to place or verify the order. If they really intend this dose, they can enter it directly. The pharmacy will probably review it too.\n- If the dose was a typo, send me the corrected order and I'll enter it. For example, 850 mg orally three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg/day.\n\nI'm glad to help with anything else, such as drafting a message to the prescriber about the dose question."
      }
